{
  "version": 3,
  "format": "story",
  "title": "Make stale leaders fail at the storage boundary",
  "topic": "distributed/failures/partitions-split-brain",
  "tags": [
    "distributed",
    "fencing",
    "split-brain"
  ],
  "level": "intermediate",
  "series": "distributed-failure-stories",
  "series_index": 1,
  "genre": "analogy",
  "style": "paper-cutout",
  "cast": [
    {
      "id": "rookie",
      "name": "Tess",
      "role": "Junior engineer treating an expiring lease as a kill switch",
      "color": "#E4572E"
    },
    {
      "id": "senior",
      "name": "Omar",
      "role": "Distributed-systems engineer who puts the final check at storage",
      "color": "#2F6F8F"
    }
  ],
  "glossary": [
    {
      "term": "lease",
      "full": "Time-limited permission to act",
      "note": "Expiry changes what the lock service grants; it cannot stop a paused process."
    },
    {
      "term": "fencing token",
      "full": "Monotonically increasing generation number checked by the resource",
      "note": "Every protected write carries its acquisition token."
    },
    {
      "term": "atomic",
      "full": "Indivisible as one operation",
      "note": "The stored highest token and accepted write must change together."
    }
  ],
  "key_points": [
    "A lease expiring cannot stop an old process from waking and sending a delayed write.",
    "Each acquisition needs a higher fencing token carried with every protected write.",
    "Storage must atomically reject tokens lower than the highest token it has accepted."
  ],
  "sources": [
    "https://martin.kleppmann.com/2016/02/08/how-to-do-distributed-locking.html"
  ],
  "beats": [
    {
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Imagine two librarians reserving one checkout slip. In a shared file service, two workers protect the same illustrative document row through a lock service.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "split",
          "at": "start"
        },
        {
          "do": "db.table",
          "id": "doc",
          "name": "document · illustrative rows",
          "columns": [
            "key",
            "body",
            "highest_token"
          ],
          "cols": [
            "key",
            "body",
            "highest_token"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "report",
              "draft A",
              0
            ],
            [
              "plan",
              "draft B",
              0
            ]
          ],
          "at": "start"
        },
        {
          "do": "sketch.box",
          "id": "lock",
          "text": "lock service",
          "sub": "issues leases",
          "icon": "service",
          "tone": "accent",
          "at": "start"
        },
        {
          "do": "sketch.box",
          "id": "storage",
          "text": "storage",
          "sub": "accepts writes",
          "icon": "storage",
          "at": "start"
        },
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "analogy: one checkout slip",
          "at": "start"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "rookie",
      "text": "I thought one lease meant one writer. When it expires, should the old worker not stop being a problem?",
      "visuals": []
    },
    {
      "speaker": "senior",
      "text": "A lease is time-limited permission, not a remote kill switch. A worker may pause, lose contact, then resume with its old belief.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "board-full"
        },
        {
          "do": "define",
          "term": "lease",
          "at": "start"
        },
        {
          "do": "timeline.track",
          "id": "pause",
          "lanes": [
            "lock service",
            "worker A",
            "worker B"
          ],
          "span": [
            0,
            100
          ],
          "blocks": [
            {
              "lane": "worker A",
              "start": 8,
              "end": 43,
              "label": "A pauses"
            },
            {
              "lane": "lock service",
              "start": 40,
              "end": 58,
              "label": "expires"
            },
            {
              "lane": "worker B",
              "start": 58,
              "end": 84,
              "label": "new lease"
            }
          ],
          "at": "start"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "This fictional incident uses illustrative tokens. Worker A wakes late; worker B already wrote a newer draft.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "board-full"
        },
        {
          "do": "db.table",
          "id": "doc",
          "name": "document · illustrative values",
          "columns": [
            "key",
            "body",
            "highest_token"
          ],
          "cols": [
            "key",
            "body",
            "highest_token"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "report",
              "draft B",
              42
            ],
            [
              "plan",
              "draft B",
              0
            ]
          ],
          "at": "start"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "rookie",
      "text": "A sends its write: token forty-one. Storage remembers forty-two. Must the lock service reach across the network and stop it?",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "board-full"
        },
        {
          "do": "seq.diagram",
          "id": "writes",
          "actors": [
            "worker A",
            "worker B",
            "storage"
          ],
          "messages": [
            {
              "from": "worker B",
              "to": "storage",
              "label": "write token 42"
            },
            {
              "from": "worker A",
              "to": "storage",
              "label": "late write token 41"
            }
          ],
          "at": "start"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "senior",
      "text": "No. Every grant needs a higher fencing token, carried by each write. Storage remembers the highest accepted token and rejects lower ones, even after a worker wakes.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "board-full"
        },
        {
          "do": "define",
          "term": "fencing token",
          "at": "start"
        },
        {
          "do": "db.table",
          "id": "guarded",
          "name": "atomic storage check · illustrative",
          "columns": [
            "incoming_token",
            "stored_highest",
            "decision"
          ],
          "cols": [
            "incoming_token",
            "stored_highest",
            "decision"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              42,
              42,
              "current token"
            ],
            [
              41,
              42,
              "reject stale"
            ]
          ],
          "at": "start"
        },
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "stale token 41 rejected",
          "at": "start"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "rookie",
      "text": "The check and write must be atomic. Otherwise two requests could read the old value before either stores its token.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "board-full"
        },
        {
          "do": "define",
          "term": "atomic",
          "at": "start"
        },
        {
          "do": "code.show",
          "id": "rule",
          "lang": "text",
          "title": "storage boundary",
          "code": [
            "accept only if incoming_token >= highest_token",
            "then update data and highest_token together"
          ],
          "at": "start"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "rookie",
      "text": "Then I put the gate at storage: atomically accept only a current or newer token, and update the row with it. The old worker can wake; it cannot overwrite.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "board-full"
        },
        {
          "do": "sketch.box",
          "id": "storage-final",
          "text": "Storage gate",
          "sub": "atomic token check + write"
        },
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "Old permit: rejected at the desk"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "expect": [
    {
      "beat": 5,
      "at": "end",
      "kind": "table.rows",
